---
layout: layouts/world.njk
title: The Hii World Model
description: An unreleased whole-system preview of the Hii World Model and its eight editorial domains.
permalink: /understand/world-model/index.html
robots: noindex, nofollow
bodyClass: world-model-preview-body
pageScript: /assets/js/world-model-preview.js
---
<div class="wm-preview-ribbon" role="status">{{ worldModelPreview.status }} · No public release data</div>

<section class="wm-map-hero section-shell">
  <aside class="wm-map-intro">
    <a class="wm-back-link" href="/understand/">← Back to Understand</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">Whole-system orientation</p>
    <h1>The Hii World Model</h1>
    <p class="lede">A living map of the AI transition and its impact on humanity. Explore how domains connect, influence one another, and evolve over time.</p>
    <details class="wm-how-it-works">
      <summary>How this model works</summary>
      <p>The map renders editorial domains and reviewed relationships from versioned records. Line treatment describes relationship trajectory, not evidence strength or overall model quality.</p>
    </details>
    <nav class="wm-map-modes" aria-label="Explore the system">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore the system</p>
      <a class="is-current" href="#world-map">World map <small>See how everything connects</small></a>
      <a href="#domain-list">Domains <small>Explore each domain in depth</small></a>
      <a href="#relationship-list">Connections <small>View candidate relationships</small></a>
      <a href="#model-boundary">Evidence <small>Understand the release boundary</small></a>
    </nav>
  </aside>

  <div id="world-map" class="wm-map-column">
    <div class="wm-radial-map" aria-label="Eight World Model domains arranged around the AI transition">
      <div class="wm-map-rings" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <svg class="wm-map-lines" viewBox="0 0 800 800" role="img" aria-label="Three candidate emerging relationships connect AI Capabilities, Human Judgment and Agency, Information Environment, and Education and Learning">
        <path class="trajectory-emerging" d="M400 128 Q565 210 642 330" />
        <path class="trajectory-emerging" d="M642 330 Q510 350 400 400" />
        <path class="trajectory-emerging" d="M400 128 Q330 420 400 672" />
      </svg>
      <div class="wm-map-center"><span>The</span><strong>AI Transition</strong><small>Editorial framing</small></div>
      {% for domain in worldModelPreview.domains %}
        <a class="wm-map-node wm-node-{{ loop.index }} tone-{{ domain.tone }}" href="/understand/world-model/domains/{{ domain.id }}/">
          <span>{{ domain.glyph }}</span>
          <strong>{{ domain.name }}</strong>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="wm-trajectory-legend" aria-label="Relationship trajectory legend">
      <span><i class="line-emerging"></i> Emerging</span>
      <span><i class="line-strengthening"></i> Strengthening</span>
      <span><i class="line-stable"></i> Stable</span>
      <span><i class="line-disputed"></i> Disputed</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="domain-list" class="wm-domain-section section-shell" aria-labelledby="domains-heading">
  <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Eight initial domains</p>
    <h2 id="domains-heading">One transition. Eight human systems in motion.</h2>
    <p>The domains are editorial lenses, not scientific truths. Their stable identities allow the model to evolve without losing continuity.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wm-domain-grid">
    {% for domain in worldModelPreview.domains %}
      <a class="wm-domain-card tone-{{ domain.tone }}" href="/understand/world-model/domains/{{ domain.id }}/">
        <span>{{ domain.glyph }}</span>
        <p>0{{ loop.index }}</p>
        <h3>{{ domain.name }}</h3>
        <small>{{ domain.short }}</small>
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="relationship-list" class="wm-relationship-section">
  <div class="section-shell wm-relationship-inner">
    <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Candidate connections</p>
      <h2>Relationships are where change becomes visible.</h2>
      <p>Only the first orientation question has a proposed evidence packet. These three connections remain unreleased.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="wm-relationship-list">
      {% for relationship in worldModelPreview.relationships %}
        {% set fromDomain = worldModelPreview.domains | findById(relationship.from) %}
        {% set toDomain = worldModelPreview.domains | findById(relationship.to) %}
        <article>
          <div class="wm-relationship-pair"><strong>{{ fromDomain.name }}</strong><span>↔</span><strong>{{ toDomain.name }}</strong></div>
          <p>{{ relationship.mechanism }}</p>
          <dl><div><dt>Trajectory</dt><dd>{{ relationship.trajectory }}</dd></div><div><dt>Strength</dt><dd>{{ relationship.strength }}</dd></div></dl>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="model-boundary" class="wm-about-model section-shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">About this preview</p>
  <h2>The public model changes only through human-reviewed releases.</h2>
  <div>
    <p>Research automation may discover sources and prepare proposals. It cannot silently rewrite the public model, create a global confidence score, or authorize publication.</p>
    <p><strong>{{ worldModelPreview.status }}</strong><br>{{ worldModelPreview.reviewed }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wm-system-close"><p>See the whole system. <span>•</span> Make sense of what is happening. <span>•</span> Stay oriented. <span>•</span> Act wisely together.</p></section>
